1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,285
Do you see a pattern?

2
00:00:01,285 --> 00:00:06,603
A metal that reacts strongly with oxygen also reacts strongly with water and dilute acids.

3
00:00:06,603 --> 00:00:12,796
So we can list metals from most reactive to least reactive: potassium, sodium, calcium, magnesium, zinc...

4
00:00:13,796 --> 00:00:16,075
...then iron, copper, silver and gold.

5
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:20,925
This list is the reactivity series, and it helps us predict how a metal will react.

6
00:00:21,983 --> 00:00:25,782
We use it every day. Steel is galvanised with a coating of zinc,

7
00:00:25,782 --> 00:00:30,514
which forms a protective oxide layer that keeps air and water away from the iron.

8
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:33,618
Catalytic converters use platinum,

9
00:00:33,618 --> 00:00:39,812
palladium and rhodium as catalysts: substances that speed up a reaction without being changed themselves.

10
00:00:39,812 --> 00:00:44,661
They turn harmful exhaust gases into less harmful ones, but these metals are rare,

11
00:00:44,661 --> 00:00:46,882
costly and mined in only a few places.

12
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:51,329
A strip of zinc is put into blue copper sulfate solution.

13
00:00:51,329 --> 00:00:55,069
A strip of copper is put into colourless zinc sulfate solution.

14
00:00:55,069 --> 00:00:58,925
Predict: in which beaker will a reaction happen? Pause and decide.

15
00:00:59,984 --> 00:01:02,788
Watch. Both beakers are left for twenty minutes.

16
00:01:03,847 --> 00:01:08,288
In the first beaker, the blue colour fades and brown copper coats the zinc.

17
00:01:08,288 --> 00:01:10,450
Nothing happens in the second beaker.

18
00:01:11,508 --> 00:01:14,839
Explain what you saw. Zinc is more reactive than copper,

19
00:01:14,839 --> 00:01:20,565
so it pushes copper out of its compound: zinc plus copper sulfate gives zinc sulfate plus copper.

20
00:01:20,565 --> 00:01:26,174
This is a displacement reaction. Copper is less reactive than zinc, so it cannot displace zinc.

21
00:01:26,174 --> 00:01:28,453
Pause and explain it in your own words.

22
00:01:29,512 --> 00:01:34,946
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

23
00:01:36,004 --> 00:01:41,204
Question 1: Write the word equation for magnesium burning in oxygen. Pause the video now.

24
00:01:42,263 --> 00:01:45,477
Answer: magnesium plus oxygen leads to magnesium oxide.

25
00:01:46,535 --> 00:01:50,976
Question 2: Why are sodium and potassium stored in oil? Pause the video now.

26
00:01:52,034 --> 00:01:55,248
Answer: They react very quickly with oxygen in the air.

27
00:01:56,306 --> 00:02:01,916
Question 3: What salt forms when zinc reacts with dilute hydrochloric acid? Pause the video now.

28
00:02:02,974 --> 00:02:05,428
Answer: Zinc chloride (plus hydrogen gas).

29
00:02:06,487 --> 00:02:10,986
Question 4: Which is more reactive: copper or magnesium? Pause the video now.

30
00:02:12,044 --> 00:02:15,375
Answer: Magnesium, it is higher in the reactivity series.
